# Vite `--mode fantasy-demo` env, loaded by `npm run dev:fantasy-demo`.
#
# Exists because passing env vars inline (`VITE_API_URL=... npm run dev`)
# is bash syntax that silently does nothing in PowerShell, and because
# .env already sets VITE_API_URL — so a shell override is fragile even
# on a POSIX shell. Vite loads .env first, then .env.<mode>, so this
# file wins deterministically on every platform.
#
# Only the API base changes. Everything else (Logto auth, Sentry) is
# inherited from .env, and the fixture server proxies every endpoint it
# doesn't override straight through to the real local core-api.
#
# Deliberately does NOT set VITE_DEMO. That flag is Kalshi-specific and
# pins the widget list to ["predictions"], which would hide the very
# widget this mode exists to screenshot. Sign in normally.
#
# No secrets here, so unlike .env this file is committed.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8788
